@page "/projects/3d-reconstruction"
@using website.Data


<ProjectPage Url="/projects/3d-reconstruction" Kicker="Academic Project · MEng">
                <p class="max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
                    My MEng group project: a 3D reconstruction framework built with industrial use in mind, such as VR simulation, live room tracking and medical imaging.
                </p>
            <!-- Project Overview -->
            <ProjectSection Title="Project Overview" Icon="fas fa-cube">
                <p class="text-gray-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
                    We built a hybrid 3D reconstruction framework that combined two approaches. Feed-forward neural networks gave us
                    accurate depth, and optimization-based models gave us globally consistent pose tracking. Each one covers a weakness
                    of the other. The aim was a pipeline that could be deployed in an industrial setting, rather than a research
                    prototype that only runs in the lab.
                </p>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Project Context</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                            <li>• <strong>Team Size:</strong> 5 engineers</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Supervisor:</strong> Dr. Sharib Ali</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Duration:</strong> Full academic year (2024/2025)</li>
                            <li>• <strong>First Phase:</strong> Background research & literature review</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Development Timeline</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                            <li>• <strong>Semester 1:</strong> Research and validation of the framework</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Semester 2:</strong> Optimizing and deploying the pipeline</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Focus:</strong> An implementation fit for industrial use</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Target Output:</strong> A deployable 3D capture system</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                </ProjectSection>

            <!-- Core Technical Problem -->
            <ProjectSection Title="The Technical Challenge" Icon="fas fa-lightbulb">

                <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line mb-6">
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Fundamental Trade-Off in 3D Reconstruction</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                        Methods that are good at depth estimation tend to drift in pose tracking. Methods that track pose
                        reliably tend to give ambiguous depth. The project set out to get around this trade-off by fusing the two.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4"><i class="fas fa-brain mr-2"></i>Feed-Forward Networks (T1)</h3>
                        <div class="space-y-3">
                            <div class="border-l-4 border-line pl-4">
                                <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Strength: Depth Estimation</h4>
                                <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Produce clean, metrically accurate depth maps with absolute scale from a single image</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="border-l-4 border-line pl-4">
                                <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Weakness: Pose Drift</h4>
                                <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Small pose errors build up over a video sequence, so the 3D model drifts</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4"><i class="fas fa-chart-line mr-2"></i>Optimization Models (T2)</h3>
                        <div class="space-y-3">
                            <div class="border-l-4 border-line pl-4">
                                <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Strength: Pose Tracking</h4>
                                <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Globally consistent pose estimates that don't drift over time</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="border-l-4 border-line pl-4">
                                <h4 class="font-semibold text-white">Weakness: Depth Ambiguity</h4>
                                <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Pseudo-depth only gives relative ordering, with no absolute scale</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                </ProjectSection>

            <!-- Novel Fusion Approach -->
            <ProjectSection Title="Novel Fusion Strategy" Icon="fas fa-code-branch">

                <div class="bg-cyan-900/20 rounded-lg p-6 border border-line mb-6">
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">The "Best of Both Worlds" Approach</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        Our hypothesis was that combining feed-forward depth estimation with optimization-based pose tracking would give
                        a system with the strengths of both, where each method makes up for the other's weakness.
                    </p>
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                        <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded p-4">
                            <p class="text-cy font-semibold mb-2">✓ FF Network fixes optimization depth ambiguity</p>
                            <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Clean, absolute-scale depth maps remove the pseudo-depth artifacts</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded p-4">
                            <p class="text-cy font-semibold mb-2">✓ Optimization fixes FF pose drift</p>
                            <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Globally consistent pose tracking stops errors from building up</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Research Phase (Semester 1)</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                            <li>• Experiments to validate the fusion method</li>
                            <li>• Benchmarking against state-of-the-art methods on HPC</li>
                            <li>• Measuring gains in accuracy and speed</li>
                            <li>• Comparison with other fusion approaches</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Deployment Phase (Semester 2)</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                            <li>• Optimizing the pipeline for deployment</li>
                            <li>• Documentation and workflow design</li>
                            <li>• Real-time 3D scene capture</li>
                            <li>• Demonstrations aimed at industrial applications</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                </ProjectSection>

            <!-- Target Applications -->
            <ProjectSection Title="Industrial Applications" Icon="fas fa-industry">

                <p class="text-gray-300 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
                    We designed the framework for use outside the lab, in industrial settings. These were the areas we had in mind,
                    each of which needs accurate 3D reconstruction in real time.
                </p>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <div class="text-4xl mb-3">🥽</div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-3">VR/AR Simulation</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">
                            Capturing 3D scenes in real time for virtual reality, for digital twins and interactive
                            simulations
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <div class="text-4xl mb-3">🏠</div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-3">Live Room Tracking</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">
                            Rebuilding a changing environment as it changes, for spatial computing, motion capture and
                            augmented reality
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <div class="text-4xl mb-3">🏥</div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-3">Medical Imaging</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">
                            Tracking surgical tools and reconstructing anatomy for computer-assisted interventions and
                            medical visualization
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                </ProjectSection>

