                    We ran the project in agile sprints, which kept progress visible and let us change course when we needed to.
                    It started with a background research phase of literature review and validating the method.
                </p>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-6">
                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-cyan-600/25">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4"><i class="fas fa-sync-alt mr-2"></i>Agile Sprint Methodology</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                            <li>• <strong>Sprint Duration:</strong> 2-week development cycles</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Sprint Planning:</strong> Breaking work into tasks and estimating them</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Daily Standups:</strong> Short check-ins on progress and blockers</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Sprint Reviews:</strong> Showing progress to our supervisor</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Retrospectives:</strong> What to change for the next sprint</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4"><i class="fas fa-columns mr-2"></i>Kanban Board Management</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                            <li>• <strong>Backlog:</strong> Feature and research tasks in priority order</li>
                            <li>• <strong>In Progress:</strong> Development and experiments under way</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Review:</strong> Code review and validation</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Done:</strong> Completed and documented work</li>
                            <li>• <strong>Blocked:</strong> Work waiting on a dependency</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="from-teal-900/30 to-cyan-900/30 rounded-lg p-6 border border-line mb-6 bg-white/[.02]">
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4"><i class="fas fa-chart-gantt mr-2"></i>Gantt Chart Timeline Planning</h3>
